  "note": "Verso body page, genuinely TWO columns down to y 0.604: Fig. 1.20 (parts a and b as one graphic) and its caption occupy the wide OUTER (left) margin column x 0.127-0.432, with the running text set in a narrow measure beside them, x 0.438-0.903. From block 13 (y 0.613) the text reverts to the single full measure x 0.314-0.903, which spans both declared columns, so those elements are column 'full'. The boundary was set by measuring the left edge each element is set to, not by where the figure happens to stop: block 12's equation still carries the narrow measure's indent (x 0.469, matching the other narrow-measure equations at x 0.472) rather than the full measure's (x 0.346), so it is column 'right' even though the figure column beside it is already empty. Mirror image of recto p027: the outer margin and the grey #d1d2d4 running-header panel ('Physics', set large at size_rel 2.25) and the page-number box are all on the left here, and the pale blue #c6eafb page_header_band covers the whole page top (y 0-0.067) with its #41c7f4 hairline and #00adef foot rule as internal edges - no separate rule_bar and no footer_rule on this page. Figure 1.20's caption is printed entirely in the chapter cyan #00adef; A2 gave no block for it, so it takes n: null while the graphic itself takes n=1. Blocks 18 and 20 ('At a point on the dipole axis', 'At a point on the equatorial plane') are italic run-in lead-ins to the equations below them; A2 typed them as paragraphs and they are kept as role paragraph with font serif-italic rather than promoted to headings. The '2022-23' edition line at the foot (y 0.956-0.963) is recorded as a running_header because the allowed role list has no footer-text role; its bbox places it at the foot. All 21 A2 blocks were matched by position."
